   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Ink Arrow\n\nA hand-drawn arrow that draws itself from one point to another in stop-motion poses.\n\nCategory: paper. Length: 5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A hand-drawn annotation should point from one thing to another: callouts over paper or scrapbook scenes.\n- The pointing itself is part of the story and should be seen being drawn, pose by pose.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You need a straight technical connector or a diagram edge: this is a wobbly pen line with a personality.\n- The arrow must follow another element's live position: the endpoints are fixed in the layout.\n\nVariables:\n- label (string): Label, default \"Start here\"\n- card_title (string): Card title, default \"The thing it points at\"\n- card_subtitle (string): Card subtitle, default \"Positioned by you, drawn by the pen\"\n- curvature (number, -1-1): Curvature, default 0.35\n- stroke_width (number, 2-24): Brush width, default 8\n- pressure (number, 0.05-1): Opening pressure, default 0.2\n- release (number, 0.05-1): Closing pressure, default 1\n- grain (number, 0-2): Grain, default 1\n- head_size (number, 8-48): Head size, default 24\n- draw_dur (number, 12-90): Draw frames, default 36\n- head_dur (number, 4-48): Head frames, default 12\n- color (color): Ink color, default \"#26242c\"\n- seed (string): Seed, default \"arrow\"\n- step (number, 1-6): Frames per pose, default 3\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
